{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BCfbVc4edi8RmRnSCJuzrj","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"ICLR 2026 reviewer guidelines rating scale scoring criteria\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"📈 ICLR 2026 Submission Storm: 19,797 Papers, New Review Rules, and the Age of AI Convergence | CSPaper Forum\",\"url\":\"https://forum.cspaper.org/topic/169/iclr-2026-submission-storm-19-797-papers-new-review-rules-and-the-age-of-ai-convergence\"},{\"title\":\"ICLR 2026 Reviewer Guide\",\"url\":\"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2026/ReviewerGuide\"},{\"title\":\"Insights from the ICLR Peer Review and Rebuttal Process\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2511.15462\"},{\"title\":\"ICML 2026 Reviewer Instructions\",\"url\":\"https://icml.cc/Conferences/2026/ReviewerInstructions\"},{\"title\":\"ICLR 2026 Scores Released: Reviewers Call It \\\"Crazy\\\", DeepMind Researchers Show Comeback from Desperate Situation\",\"url\":\"https://eu.36kr.com/en/p/3551362253731718\"},{\"title\":\"ICLR 2026 Area Chair Guide\",\"url\":\"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2026/AreaChairGuide\"},{\"title\":\"PaperDecision | Modeling the Complete Peer Review Process\",\"url\":\"https://paperdecision.netlify.app/\"},{\"title\":\"WHAT DRIVES PAPER ACCEPTANCE? A PROCESS- CENTRIC ANALYSIS OF MODERN PEER REVIEW\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2509.25701\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about ICLR 2026 reviewer guidelines:\n\n## Rating Scale\n\nThe overall rating for ICLR 2026 is mapped to {0, 2, 4, 6, 8, 10}, which represents a change from previous years. The new 2–4–6–8–10 system removes the middle ground, forcing reviewers into decisive opinions.\n\n## Scoring Criteria\n\nNumerical scores are provided for soundness, presentation, contribution, confidence, and overall rating.\n\nThe new formula reviewers adopt is: Novelty × Depth × Presentation × Reproducibility ≈ Weak Accept+\n\n## Additional Guidelines\n\nReviews are expected to be timely and substantive, and reviewers must follow the reviewing guidelines. The official ICLR 2026 Reviewer Guide is available at iclr.cc/Conferences/2026/ReviewerGuide, which contains further details on the decision process and reviewer expectations.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f47ef9e2-3bdc-4328-afa5-da8117d03f95","uuid":"58852d34-3929-4cc5-8db7-b913ce2fa956","timestamp":"2026-05-21T05:10:39.435Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"ICLR 2026 reviewer guidelines rating scale scoring criteria","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01JYoK7jyGWbWW1FYwi4U3X8","content":[{"title":"📈 ICLR 2026 Submission Storm: 19,797 Papers, New Review Rules, and the Age of AI Convergence | CSPaper Forum","url":"https://forum.cspaper.org/topic/169/iclr-2026-submission-storm-19-797-papers-new-review-rules-and-the-age-of-ai-convergence"},{"title":"ICLR 2026 Reviewer Guide","url":"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2026/ReviewerGuide"},{"title":"Insights from the ICLR Peer Review and Rebuttal Process","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2511.15462"},{"title":"ICML 2026 Reviewer Instructions","url":"https://icml.cc/Conferences/2026/ReviewerInstructions"},{"title":"ICLR 2026 Scores Released: Reviewers Call It \"Crazy\", DeepMind Researchers Show Comeback from Desperate Situation","url":"https://eu.36kr.com/en/p/3551362253731718"},{"title":"ICLR 2026 Area Chair Guide","url":"https://iclr.cc/Conferences/2026/AreaChairGuide"},{"title":"PaperDecision | Modeling the Complete Peer Review Process","url":"https://paperdecision.netlify.app/"},{"title":"WHAT DRIVES PAPER ACCEPTANCE? A PROCESS- CENTRIC ANALYSIS OF MODERN PEER REVIEW","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2509.25701"}]},"Based on the search results, here's what I found about ICLR 2026 reviewer guidelines:\n\n## Rating Scale\n\nThe overall rating for ICLR 2026 is mapped to {0, 2, 4, 6, 8, 10}, which represents a change from previous years. The new 2–4–6–8–10 system removes the middle ground, forcing reviewers into decisive opinions.\n\n## Scoring Criteria\n\nNumerical scores are provided for soundness, presentation, contribution, confidence, and overall rating.\n\nThe new formula reviewers adopt is: Novelty × Depth × Presentation × Reproducibility ≈ Weak Accept+\n\n## Additional Guidelines\n\nReviews are expected to be timely and substantive, and reviewers must follow the reviewing guidelines. The official ICLR 2026 Reviewer Guide is available at iclr.cc/Conferences/2026/ReviewerGuide, which contains further details on the decision process and reviewer expectations."],"durationSeconds":6.144076404}}
