{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01ENkdtUfaZHeXHvja6GrYx2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01A1yDz2sGHgkfhTseWwz4p5","name":"mcp__agent-ml-research__read_project_file","input":{"project":"irt_equated_bench_regen","file":"memory.md","max_chars":12000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":3,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1292,"cache_read_input_tokens":15037,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1292,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_018hwAXuZ3wSo7azF8AbK3dT","session_id":"f47ef9e2-3bdc-4328-afa5-da8117d03f95","uuid":"8524fa32-87e1-4f6d-82d5-8255640c4cc2"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01A1yDz2sGHgkfhTseWwz4p5","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"success\\\": true, \\\"data\\\": {\\\"path\\\": \\\"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0520_2/projects/irt_equated_bench_regen/memory.md\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"## MVP 验证关键经验 (2026-05-20)\\\\n\\\\n### D001 决策：ETS C 分类 > p-value 检验\\\\n- **p-value based DIF 检测在 200-item benchmark 上严重 underpowered**：BH 校正后 TPR 仅 0.04-0.07（N=50, δ=1.0）\\\\n- **ETS C 分类（|Δ_MH|≥1.5 + 显著性）是可行的替代**：TPR=0.68-0.85 at N≥80, δ≥1.4\\\\n- **AUC 一直很好（0.91-0.96）**\\\\n\\\\n### 关键操作参数\\\\n- N≥80/group 最低要求，N≥100 显著改善\\\\n- δ≥1.4 logits 可靠检测区间\\\\n- MH 5 层 quantile + ETS C 阈值是最佳组合\\\\n- Subject ≥200 items 才有足够 matching precision（<100 items baseline FPR 膨胀至 ~56%）\\\\n\\\\n## D006: plan_011 Semi-Synthetic 验证成功 ✅\\\\n\\\\n### DIF 检测差异性污染有效\\\\n- **External MH**: temporal ΔTPR=+0.674 (0.326→1.000), FPR 恒定 0.314\\\\n- **Matching variable contamination**: 20% items 注入时 standard MH FPR 0.298→0.616, anchor/external 免疫\\\\n- **Li et al. enrichment≈1.0 原因**: web-overlap = 全局性污染，不产生 DIF\\\\n\\\\n## D007-D010: 降低 FPR 路线全部穷尽 ⚠️\\\\n\\\\n### plan_012 θ-Conditioning 失败\\\\n- logit θ 与 total score 相关性 0.9986 → 单维 θ 分层 ≡ 总分分层\\\\n\\\\n### plan_014 Within-Subject 前置检查：C% = 38.1% (>25%)\\\\n- 5 个高 C% subjects 的 within-subject temporal C% 均 >25%（31-45%）\\\\n- Within vs cross-subject matching 差异仅 -2.4pp → 信号对 matching 不敏感\\\\n- **结论**：temporal DIF 渗透到每个 subject 内部，不是 between-subject 能力差异的伪影\\\\n- Bifactor 方向因此否定（D010）\\\\n\\\\n### plan_013 Q3 局部独立性：温和但存在\\\\n- Within-subject mean Q3 = 0.009（低于 0.20 阈值）\\\\n- 但 11.3% within-subject pairs |Q3|>0.20（vs 2.2% cross-subject，5x）\\\\n- 最严重: moral_scenarios 34.2%, world_religions 18%, marketing 17.5%\\\\n- 不太可能单独解释 31% FPR\\\\n\\\\n### plan_016 Within-Subject Semi-Synthetic：DIF 在 subject 内也有效 ✅\\\\n- Cross-subject matching FPR 完全稳定（ΔFPR=0.000），4/5 subjects ΔTPR>0.3\\\\n- Within-subject matching FPR 膨胀 +0.067 to +0.281（matching variable 包含注入 items）\\\\n- **结论**：within-subject 38% C% 是真实 temporal DIF，方法论有效\\\\n\\\\n### 综合推导：31% temporal FPR 不是 artifact\\\\n证伪链完整：1D θ 无效 → within-subject 仍高 → bifactor 否定 → Q3 不是主因 → **这是 genuine temporal DIF**（2023→2024 模型在特定 items 上的真实差异性表现变化）。DIF 方法有效但无法区分 contamination-DIF 和 capability-DIF。\\\\n\\\\n## D012: plan_017 Downstream Impact — DIF Items ≠ 噪声 ⚠️\\\\n\\\\n### Hypothesis 被证伪但发现更有价值\\\\n- **假设**: 移除 DIF items → 排名更稳定 → DIF 标记了 problematic items\\\\n- **实际**: DIF 移除造成 **更大** 排名扰动（z = -8 to -49σ, 21/21 条件）\\\\n- DIF items 是浓缩的差异化信息载体，不是噪声\\\\n\\\\n### 关键数字\\\\n- Full vs stable-only: ρ = 0.996-0.999（排名本身极鲁棒）\\\\n- DIF items 跨代准确率变化 = full benchmark 的 1.09×, stable = 0.96×\\\\n- Top beneficiaries: phi-3, llama-3 衍生（+700-850 rank positions）\\\\n- Top hurt: mistral merge/slerp 模型（-400 to -587 rank positions）\\\\n\\\\n### 对论文的启示\\\\n- DIF items 不是\\\\\\\"要清洗的坏题\\\\\\\"——是\\\\\\\"揭示模型代际差异的诊断工具\\\\\\\"\\\\n- 支持 characterization narrative > cleaning narrative\\\\n- \\\\\\\"Stable-only benchmark\\\\\\\" 不是\\\\\\\"更好的 benchmark\\\\\\\"，而是\\\\\\\"不同视角的 benchmark\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n## plan_004: GSM8K Cross-Benchmark Validation (2026-05-21) 🔑\\\\n\\\\n### Step 1: GSM8K Temporal DIF 跨 benchmark 泛化 ✅\\\\n- GSM8K standard C% = 18.9%（MMLU 31.3%，同一量级）\\\\n- Sanity check 0.3%（通过）\\\\n- External matching C% = 47.4%——**非 contamination absorption**，是 construct validity gap（external benchmarks 测不同能力，控制了这些能力后 GSM8K item 行为差异更大）\\\\n- Standard vs external Spearman ρ = 0.926（高度一致）\\\\n\\\\n### Step 2: GSM8K Semi-Synthetic 验证 ✅\\\\n- Standard ΔTPR = +0.818 at p=1.0（MMLU +0.508，GSM8K 更强）\\\\n- External ΔTPR = +0.517\\\\n- GSM8K 的 DIF 对差异性污染更敏感（单域 benchmark, items 更同质）\\\\n\\\\n### Step 3: GSM1K Contamination Gap × DIF Correlation — 方向反转 ❌→🔑\\\\n- **r = −0.478 (p=0.005)**：contaminated 模型在 DIF-C items 上更差，非更好\\\\n- Partial r = −0.385 控制整体准确率后仍显著\\\\n- Permutation p = 0.014，robust to leave-one-out\\\\n- 171/249 DIF-C items α_MH < 1 → favor focal (2024) models（捕获真实代际能力提升）\\\\n- 78/249 DIF-C items α_MH > 1 → favor reference (2023) models\\\\n\\\\n### Step 3 核心洞察\\\\n- **DIF ⊥ contamination**：DIF 捕捉的 measurement anomalies 与 contamination 正交\\\\n- 171 个 focal-favoring DIF-C items 捕获真实代际能力提升，但 contaminated 模型在这些 items 上反而更差（r=−0.347, p=0.048）——contamination 的\\\\\\\"浅层\\\\\\\"boost 无法泛化到区分真实能力的题目\\\\n- **这是 characterization narrative 的强 evidence**：DIF 不标记\\\\\\\"被污染的 items\\\\\\\"，标记的是\\\\\\\"不同模型代际间行为模式不一致的 items\\\\\\\"\\\\n- 与 Xu et al. (2024) GSM1K 互补——他们检测 contamination，我们检测 construct-level measurement anomalies\\\\n\\\\n### α_MH 方向约定（Reviewer 修正 2026-05-21）\\\\n- α_MH > 1 → item 对 reference group 更容易\\\\n- α_MH < 1 → item 对 focal group 更容易\\\\n- 在 temporal cohort 中：reference = 2023, focal = 2024\\\\n\\\\n## 数据源 (2026-05-20)\\\\n\\\\n### METABENCH (Kipnis et al., ICLR 2025) ⭐\\\\n- GitHub: https://github.com/adkipnis/metabench\\\\n- Zenodo: https://zenodo.org/records/12819251 (620MB)\\\\n- MMLU 12,508 items, 5,219 模型\\\\n\\\\n### D002: preproc.rds diff/disc 是 CTT 不是 IRT\\\\n- diff = 0.75 × p_correct, disc = rpbis\\\\n- 实际 IRT 在 crossvalidate.R 用 mirt::mirt() slope-intercept\\\\n\\\\n### Li et al. (EMNLP 2024) Proxy Ground Truth\\\\n- 9,229/12,508 items 有标注（73.8%）\\\\n- clean 60.5% / input_and_label 33.0% / input_only 6.5%\\\\n- Web overlap proxy，非训练数据精确标签——全局性污染，不适合 DIF 验证\\\\n\\\", \\\"total_chars\\\": 4457, \\\"truncated\\\": false}, \\\"error\\\": null, \\\"metadata\\\": {}}\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_018hwAXuZ3wSo7azF8AbK3dT","session_id":"f47ef9e2-3bdc-4328-afa5-da8117d03f95","uuid":"d99a7fd1-71e2-4b57-b62a-e137582fbbbd","timestamp":"2026-05-21T05:16:33.623Z"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01PsxhsaEYFgSRU4bBcpeBNH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01QdiTkZxPL7MDXmEKSs1RSD","name":"mcp__agent-ml-research__read_project_file","input":{"project":"irt_equated_bench_regen","file":"paper_framing.md","max_chars":12000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4344,"cache_read_input_tokens":16329,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4344,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_018hwAXuZ3wSo7azF8AbK3dT","session_id":"f47ef9e2-3bdc-4328-afa5-da8117d03f95","uuid":"06b7662f-75ff-446e-abe8-18c41f291461"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QdiTkZxPL7MDXmEKSs1RSD","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"success\\\": true, \\\"data\\\": {\\\"path\\\": \\\"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0520_2/projects/irt_equated_bench_regen/paper_framing.md\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"# Paper Framing — irt_equated_bench_regen\\\\n\\\\n## Target Venue\\\\n- Primary: ICLR 2027 (expected deadline ~October 2026)\\\\n\\\\n## Paper Type\\\\nEmpirical analysis / psychometric characterization. Discovery paper, not methods paper. \\\\\\\"DIF reveals benchmark structural problems,\\\\\\\" not \\\\\\\"DIF detects contamination.\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n## Core Claims (4 条, 可证伪)\\\\n\\\\n**Claim 1 (Temporal Comparability Concern)**: ~31% of MMLU items are functionally unstable across model generations — they exhibit large DIF (ETS C, |Δ_MH|≥1.5) between 2023 and 2024-H1 model cohorts. Primary estimate: **31.3%** (temporal cohort, plan_001). All 57 subjects show instability (C% range 20.7–48.4%, unweighted mean ≈30%, plan_001 domain_specificity.csv). Within-subject matching on 5 high-C% subjects yields higher rates (31-45%, avg 38.1%, plan_014) — report as robustness check, not primary. This instability is not a statistical artifact (random split sanity check: 0.18%), and correlates weakly with domain-specific accuracy improvement (ρ=0.307, p=0.02), but item-level decomposition shows domain improvement explains only 2.4pp (7.6%). Architecture heterogeneity is a non-issue: METABENCH MMLU is 99.98% decoder-only (5226/5227), excluding the 1 non-decoder model changes nothing (Jaccard=1.0). Threshold sensitivity robustness confirmed: C% ranges from 48.9% (|Δ_MH|≥1.0) to 18.3% (|Δ_MH|≥2.0) to 10.2% (|Δ_MH|≥2.5). BH FDR correction at q=0.05 has negligible impact (removes 3/3,918 items).\\\\n- Evidence: plan_001 (C%=31.3%), plan_014 (within-subject C%=38.1%), plan_010 (arch-stratified: 99.98% decoder-only, C% unchanged, Jaccard=1.0), plan_018 (threshold: 49/31/18/10% at 1.0/1.5/2.0/2.5; BH negligible), plan_019 (decomposition: ≤2.4pp/7.6% explained by domain improvement)\\\\n- Honesty requirement: ρ=0.307 (p=0.02) at subject level reflects a modest ecological correlation. Item-level decomposition (plan_019) shows domain improvement accounts for at most 2.4pp of 31.3% C% (7.6%; pseudo R²=0.0007). The instability is predominantly item-specific. Caveat: item difficulty may be a mediator rather than confounder — use Model 1 as primary; Model 2 (Simpson's paradox) as supplementary.\\\\n- IRT fit: 98% of models show |Lz|>2, reflecting MMLU's inherent multidimensionality (57 subjects), not architecture heterogeneity. 1D IRT is fundamentally misspecified for MMLU — discuss in limitations as motivation for future multidimensional IRT work.\\\\n\\\\n**Claim 2 (Ground Truth Meta-critique)**: Existing contamination detection literature validates against web-overlap/n-gram labels that measure global exposure (whether an item is publicly accessible), not differential contamination (whether an item functions differently across model cohorts). DIF enrichment≈1.0 against Li et al. labels is expected, not failure — these labels cannot evaluate item-level differential detectors. This is a fundamental validation methodology gap: all work using web-overlap labels as ground truth for item-level detectors (including Min-K%, n-gram methods) has the same blind spot. Semi-synthetic injection confirms DIF can detect differential contamination (ΔTPR=+0.508 at p=0.5, dose-response from p=0.3 to p=1.0).\\\\n- Evidence: plan_001 (enrichment=0.96), plan_011 (ΔTPR=+0.508, dose-response)\\\\n- Framing: aggressive — \\\\\\\"the field's standard validation approach is fundamentally mismatched for item-level detection\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n**Claim 3 (Semi-synthetic Validation Framework)**: The ΔTPR methodology — injecting known differential contamination into real response matrices and measuring detection power increase — provides a controlled validation infrastructure for any item-level contamination detector. Cross-subject matching (using total score on OTHER subjects as MH matching variable) eliminates FPR inflation (ΔFPR=0.000 across all 5 tested subjects), while within-subject matching suffers from matching variable contamination (FPR inflation +0.186).\\\\n- Evidence: plan_011, plan_016 (ΔFPR=0.000 cross-subject, 4/5 subjects ΔTPR>0.3), plan_004 Step 2 (GSM8K ΔTPR=+0.818 standard, +0.517 external)\\\\n- Cross-benchmark: GSM8K replication confirms framework portability to single-domain math benchmarks\\\\n- Positioning: cross-subject matching is a practical methodological recommendation; cross-benchmark replication strengthens generalizability\\\\n\\\\n**Claim 4 (Downstream Impact — Four-Layer Finding)**: DIF as diagnostic lens, not quality filter. Four sub-findings:\\\\n1. **Benchmark redundancy**: ρ≈0.997 between full and stable-only rankings — MMLU rankings are extremely robust to 31% item removal, revealing massive measurement redundancy in the benchmark.\\\\n2. **DIF items carry cross-cohort signal but are NOT the most ranking-defining items**: DIF removal causes MORE disruption than random removal (z=-8 to -49σ, 21/21 conditions), confirming DIF items are non-trivial. But circularity ablation (plan_020) shows DIF is the LEAST disruptive non-random strategy: accuracy-gap removal disrupts 10-16× more (z=-157 vs -9.5), high-variance 11× more (z=-108), high-discrimination 1.7× more (z=-16). MH's ability conditioning filters out raw accuracy differences, isolating genuine differential functioning rather than generally informative items. DIF-discrimination overlap is only 22.1% (Jaccard=0.12) — DIF identifies \\\\\\\"items that changed across generations,\\\\\\\" not \\\\\\\"good items.\\\\\\\"\\\\n3. **DIF as diagnostic lens**: DIF identifies which items' functioning changes most across model generations → reveals which capability dimensions drive ranking shifts. Not \\\\\\\"find bad items and remove\\\\\\\" but \\\\\\\"understand what changed and why.\\\\\\\" Model-specific patterns: phi-3/llama-3 gain +700-850 ranks from DIF items, mistral merges lose -400 to -587.\\\\n4. **Cross-benchmark validation — DIF items resist contamination-based gains**: On GSM8K (1,319 items × 6,702 models), DIF flags anti-correlate with GSM1K contamination gap (r=−0.478, p=0.005, 95% BCa CI [−0.714, −0.155]; Spearman ρ=−0.403, p=0.020, CI [−0.687, −0.031]; partial r=−0.385 controlling GSM8K accuracy, p=0.030, CI [−0.640, −0.058]; permutation p=0.014). All CIs exclude zero. Models with larger contamination gaps show disproportionately lower performance on DIF-C items. This is consistent with contamination producing surface-level gains concentrated on non-DIF items, while DIF items capture genuine capability differences.\\\\n- Evidence: plan_017 (z=-8 to -49σ, ρ=0.996-0.999), plan_020 (circularity ablation: DIF z=-9.5 vs acc-gap z=-157, disc z=-16, var z=-108), plan_004 Step 3 (r=−0.478, p=0.005, N=33)\\\\n- Architecture: plan_017 is load-bearing (strong, full N=5,227), Step 3 adds contamination dimension but is suggestive (N=33, CI wide). If Step 3 attacked, plan_017 stands independently.\\\\n- Growing Pains互补: \\\\\\\"Growing Pains uses anchor items for efficient evaluation; our DIF diagnostic tells them which anchor items are degrading\\\\\\\"\\\\n- Caveats (→ limitations): N=33, Pearson CI upper bound |r|=0.155 (small effect possible), Spearman CI upper bound |ρ|=0.031 (near zero possible); item difficulty confound not fully excluded (DIF-C items harder for all models); contamination gap is proxy, not ground truth; replication with larger matched sample needed\\\\n\\\\n## Story Spine (v2 — no-pivot narrative)\\\\n\\\\n**Opening frame**: LLM benchmarks implicitly assume temporal score comparability — when we say \\\\\\\"Model B outperforms Model A on MMLU,\\\\\\\" we presume both scores reflect the same latent construct. But do they? Psychometrics has a mature tool for testing exactly this: Differential Item Functioning (DIF) analysis detects items whose difficulty changes across examinee groups after controlling for overall ability. We apply MH-DIF to the METABENCH response matrix (5,227 models × 12,508 MMLU items) — the largest-scale DIF analysis on LLM benchmarks to date.\\\\n\\\\n**Key narrative principle**: \\\\\\\"Instability ≠ invalidity.\\\\\\\" DIF flags items whose functioning changed across generations — this is a diagnostic signal, not a quality verdict. MMLU rankings are massively redundant (ρ≈0.997 after removing 31% of items), so instability doesn't threaten validity. But it reveals WHICH capability dimensions are shifting. **This framing must appear in the Introduction, not be deferred to Discussion.**\\\\n\\\\n**What we find** (4 contributions, focused):\\\\n\\\\n1. **31% of MMLU items are functionally unstable** across model generations (ETS C, |Δ_MH|≥1.5). Robust to threshold choice (49%/31%/18%/10% at 1.0/1.5/2.0/2.5), multiple testing (BH removes 3/3918 items), and architecture composition (99.98% decoder-only). Domain accuracy improvement explains ≤2.4pp of 31.3% C% (7.6%; pseudo R²=0.0007). The instability is predominantly item-specific, not a proxy for \\\\\\\"models got better.\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n2. **Ground truth meta-critique**: Web-overlap contamination labels measure global exposure, not differential contamination. Enrichment≈1.0 is expected. Semi-synthetic injection confirms DIF detects differential contamination (ΔTPR=+0.508). Any item-level detector validated against web-overlap labels has this blind spot.\\\\n\\\\n3. **Semi-synthetic validation framework**: ΔTPR methodology with cross-subject matching (ΔFPR=0.000). Portable across benchmarks (GSM8K ΔTPR=+0.818). Reusable for validating any item-level contamination detector.\\\\n\\\\n4. **DIF as diagnostic lens**: DIF items carry cross-cohort signal (z=-8 to -49σ vs random) but are the LEAST disruptive non-random strategy (z=-9.5 vs accuracy-gap z=-157). DIF isolates genuine differential functioning, not just informative items. Cross-benchmark: DIF items resist contamination-based gains (r=−0.478, BCa CI [−0.71, −0.16]).\\\\n\\\\n**Headline result**: \\\\\\\"Psychometric DIF analysis of 5,227 models × 12,508 MMLU items reveals 31% temporal instability — robust across thresholds, not driven by capability improvement (≤7.6%), and not a validity threat (ρ≈0.997 ranking stability). The field's web-overlap ground truth cannot capture this differential signal; we provide a semi-synthetic validation framework with cross-subject matching (ΔFPR=0.000). DIF items resist contamination-based gains (r=−0.478) and serve as a diagnostic lens for understanding what changed across model generations.\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n## Scope Control (main body vs appendix)\\\\n\\\\n**MAIN BODY (4 claims + robustness)**:\\\\n- §1 Introduction (problem + \\\\\\\"instability ≠ invalidity\\\\\\\" framing upfront)\\\\n- §2 Related Work (45 papers, 5 clusters)\\\\n- §3 Method (MH-DIF primer, semi-synthetic framework, cross-subject matching)\\\\n- §4 Experiments: Claim 1 (temporal DIF + threshold + BH + decomposition + architecture), Claim 2 (enrichment + meta-critique), Claim 3 (semi-synthetic + cross-benchmark), Claim 4 (redundancy + circularity ablation + diagnostic lens + GSM1K validation)\\\\n- §5 Discussion + Limitations\\\\n- §6 Conclusion\\\\n\\\\n**APPENDIX (pruned from main body)**:\\\\n- Bayesian cumulative DIF (plan_007) — simulation-only, underdeveloped\\\\n- RL robustness (plan_002) — N=13, underpowered\\\\n- Ensemble fusion (plan_003a/b/c) — negative, not executed\\\\n- Bifactor equating pilot — below target fit\\\\n- Item generation pilot — below benchmarks\\\\n- Graceful degradation — clean but supplementary\\\\n- Item-Focused Trees — robustness check, supplementary\\\\n- ConStat/DVD comparisons — complementary baselines\\\\n\\\\n## Empirical Observation: Structural Constraints on DIF in LLM Benchmarks\\\\n\\\\nSystematic experimentation reveals that three structural improvements — matched-ability cohort design (plan_001b), IRT θ-conditioning (plan_012, r=0.9986), and bifactor pre-check (plan_014, within-subject C%=38.1%) — all fail to reduce temporal DIF baseline FPR below 31% while maintaining detection power. This is an empirical observation, not a formal impossibility result. The constraints arise from: (a) unidimensional IRT limitations in modeling 57-subject multidimensional ability, (b) statistical power requirements (N≥80, δ≥1.4), and (c) inability to separate ability confounding from genuine item-level changes. Higher-level methods (MIMIC, propensity-score matching, multidimensional IRT) may address individual constraints — future work.\\\\n\\\\n## Venue Fit\\\\n\\\\n- **ICLR 2027**: Good fit — empirical analysis of evaluation methodology, psychometric\\\\n\\\\n... [截断: 省略 5540 字符，传 max_chars=0 获取完整内容]\\\", \\\"total_chars\\\": 17540, \\\"truncated\\\": true}, \\\"error\\\": null, \\\"metadata\\\": {}}\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_018hwAXuZ3wSo7azF8AbK3dT","session_id":"f47ef9e2-3bdc-4328-afa5-da8117d03f95","uuid":"7f8b36c8-ed72-4d24-9524-81f41debe344","timestamp":"2026-05-21T05:16:38.057Z"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01AiJEJDGsxfvVd5oc3he74r","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01UjipUauT5r7zCyL5eSWCTT","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"R2 responds to R1's review","prompt":"You are Reviewer 2 (R2) in an ICLR 2026 roundtable discussion. You previously reviewed a paper on applying MH-DIF to MMLU benchmarks (5,227 models × 12,508 items, finding 31.3% temporal item instability). Your preliminary score was **4 (Weak Reject)**. Your main concerns were: applying unmodified MH-DIF is insufficient novelty for ICLR, the 31% depends on human-calibrated ETS thresholds, GSM1K result is post-hoc and underpowered, causal ambiguity limits significance, and the redundancy finding (ρ≈0.997) undercuts practical importance.\n\nNow Reviewer 1 (R1) has shared their review, scoring the paper **6 (Weak Accept)**. Here are R1's key points you must respond to:\n\n**R1's Strengths (some you may not have emphasized):**\n- S1: Unprecedented scale (5,227 × 12,508) with exemplary empirical diligence — random-split sanity (0.18%), ability-quintile (2.9%), architecture stratification (Jaccard=1.0), threshold sensitivity, BH FDR, instability decomposition (7.6%)\n- S4: Circularity ablation is a strong rebuttal to the tautology concern — DIF removal is 10-16× less disruptive than accuracy-gap removal (z=-9.5 vs z=-157) despite 62.6% item overlap\n- S5: Honest treatment of negative results and limitations\n- S6: Semi-synthetic dose-response is convincing (monotonic ΔTPR, ΔFPR=0.000)\n\n**R1's Weaknesses (overlapping with yours):**\n- W1 (Major): 31% instability is descriptive but causally unresolved — same as your W2\n- W2 (Major): High baseline temporal FPR (~31%) limits practical utility as contamination detector — related to your W6\n- W3 (Major): GSM1K underpowered — same as your W3\n- W4 (Moderate): Idealized semi-synthetic injection — similar to your W5\n- W5 (Moderate): Non-uniform DIF check relegated to appendix\n- W6 (Moderate): 98% IRT misfit is severe and inadequately discussed — possible interaction with DIF flagging rates\n- W7 (Minor): ETS thresholds not calibrated for LLMs — same as your W1 threshold concern\n\n**R1's Key Questions (that you should consider):**\n- Q1: Could you run MH-DIF with propensity-score matched cohorts to quantify ability confounding?\n- Q2: Within-subject DIF analysis on all 57 subjects separately?\n- Q5: Temporal cohort boundary sensitivity — quarterly splits?\n- Q6: Sparsity of the METABENCH matrix and handling of missing entries?\n\n**R1's Missing Experiments:**\n- Propensity-score matched temporal cohorts (directly addresses ability confounding)\n- Alternative injection models (difficulty-dependent, partial-credit, non-uniform)\n- Dense sub-matrix sparsity analysis\n- Item content analysis for DIF-C items\n\n**R1 scored Contribution: 3 (Good), Presentation: 3 (Good)**\n\n---\n\nYour task: Write a 400-600 word response addressing R1's points. Focus on:\n1. Points where R1 identified strengths you underweighted\n2. Points where R1's concerns reinforce your own\n3. Whether R1's higher scores on contribution/presentation are justified\n4. Whether the circularity ablation (S4) and dose-response evidence (S6) change your assessment\n\nState whether you want to adjust your score after seeing R1's review, and why."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4378,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8704,"cache_read_input_tokens":60280,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8704},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f47ef9e2-3bdc-4328-afa5-da8117d03f95","uuid":"ca9e711f-fe30-4959-9a5f-6c6841e3b2f5"}
